# RFC-TRADECORE-0026 PTCS Renderer Gate Owner Fix

## Background

- COMM correlation: `rfc-tradecore-0026-ptcs-renderer-gate-20260922`.
- Consumer gate uses Contracts `0.1.13`, Interactive.Client `0.1.25`, Renderer `0.1.30`, true MDCQ 3820 base bars and seven rows.
- Reported owner defects: cache rehydrate preserves authoritative identity/revision but does not repaint; legend readers are globally indexed instead of row-qualified; 48-to-All rebuild creates excessive candle DOM and blocks Chrome.

## Goal

Complete the PTCS Dynamic owner package so cache hits paint bars, each row legend reads its own traces, and the 3820-by-7 browser workflow remains responsive without changing authoritative cache identity semantics.

## Assumptions

- The fix belongs in the Renderer package unless bounded source inspection proves a contract change is required.
- Runtime cache identity and `DataRevision` remain server-authoritative and must not be rewritten merely to force a repaint.
- Full-range rendering must preserve visible data semantics; performance cannot be obtained by dropping source data or cursor fidelity.

## Plan

1. Reproduce and inspect the three owner defects with bounded source/test reads.
2. Add focused unit/renderer regression coverage before or alongside the minimal implementation.
3. Implement cache payload change detection, row-local legend lookup, and bounded SVG candle rendering.
4. Run owner build/tests and the Daedalus 3820-by-7 Playwright gate where available.
5. Update RFC/current-state/Test/Verification/DevLog, version and publish exact owner packages.
6. Commit/push and report exact versions/commit through the originating COMM correlation.

## Scope

- `src/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Renderer`
- packaging consumers only where required to carry the new renderer asset
- focused owner tests and Dynamic documentation

## Acceptance

- Browser cache rehydrate paints non-zero bars while preserving authoritative identity/revision.
- Row legends use their row-specific readers.
- All/48/pan remain responsive at 3820 bars x 7 rows; pointer-to-form p95 is below 50 ms, no sustained >100 ms long task, and no browser crash in the formal gate.
- Exact package versions and commit are published and sent to Daedalus.

## Risks

- WebSharper DOM generation changes can alter marker/cursor geometry; desktop/mobile visual and cursor tests remain required.
- Release builds may auto-push packages; use Debug validation until version and source are final.

